# Allowlist, not a denylist. Everything Claude Code writes into ~/.claude
# (sessions/, cache/, telemetry/, projects/, backups/, ...) is machine-local
# runtime state, and projects/ holds full conversation transcripts. Naming
# those directories one by one would go stale the moment Claude Code adds a
# new one, so ignore everything and re-include only the two tracked files.
#
# A directory has to be un-ignored before a file inside it can be, hence the
# separate `!.claude/` line — git never descends into an excluded directory.
# See https://git-scm.com/docs/gitignore

*
!.gitignore
!.stow-local-ignore
!.claude/
!.claude/settings.json
